  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying which lottery is more right-skewed (favoring options with higher probability on unfavorable outcomes). However, the individual considers the high probability of a favorable outcome (80% for 4000 Euros) and the absence of losses as key factors—this reflects a preference for left-skewed outcomes, not right-skewed ones. The individual’s reasoning contradicts the decision reason, which would favor more right-skewed lotteries (with higher probability on bad outcomes), whereas the individual is attracted to a high chance of a good outcome. There is no mention or implication of evaluating the skewness of the distributions, nor any preference for options with concentration on unfavorable results. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based reason; in fact, their reasoning goes in the opposite direction. The information considered and the justification are entirely unrelated to the concept of right-skewness as defined.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
